        "created_at": "2025-07-20T06:47:32.607339+00:00",
        "notes": "Round 5 we see the build start to come together with the addition of  [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4).  I'm a big fan recently of the additional burst it provides and it's been treating me a lot better than other powers at this stage.\n\nItems:\n\n\u27e1  [Caduceus Ex](item_9e7965ea-2abc-44a7-b042-950c6ad2fce7) provides decent WP percentage, but I'm really looking at the extended range to beam here.  At this point in the game distancing yourself from your teammates is CRUCIAL to staying alive especially if you didn't take Serenity in round 3.  It helps you not only stay further back and around cover, but combo'd with Triage you can attach to your teammates and potentially save their life much quicker than you would without it.\n\nIn addition to Cad Ex, you have 3 other good choices to either pair with if you have the cash or grab instead.\n\n\u27e1 If you're struggling to pick up a res,  [Resurrection Rangefinder](item_99baffec-51b5-42e4-be61-e29f3de8219f) can help you res from a safer distance or pull off that risky sling res.\n\n\u27e1 If you need more survivability,  [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) grants strong passive self regen and combos well with Serenity and Angeleisure Wear.\n\n\u27e1 If you're able to push damage boost more,  [Chain Evoker](item_812cc89e-feb0-47d0-9e03-9d8e33a80aca) is a must have pocket pick.  The extra boost helps your dps secure kills and the ult charge it provides is killer for building valk fast.  Not to mention if you have Crep Circle the constant blue beams on your teammates make your ult a nuke \u0d26\u0d4d\u0d26\u0d3f \u2022\u2a4a\u2022 ).",
